      "content": "Even though it's over-the-counter, combining ibuprofen with aspirin can increase your risk of stomach upset and bleeding, which is a serious consideration for you. Since your back pain is severe, try taking extra-strength acetaminophen (Tylenol) instead, as it typically doesn't interact with aspirin in the same way. If the pain persists, try applying a heating pad to the area while you wait for your appointment.",
