      "content": "While spacing them out might seem like a strategy, it doesn't completely eliminate the risk of interaction, and your past experience doesn't guarantee future safety. For severe pain when other options fail, consider using a topical NSAID cream, which can target the back pain locally without affecting your whole system as much. If the pain is unbearable, you should consider a short-term, low-dose prescription option from a pharmacist who can provide immediate advice.",
